  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUPPORT TO ADOLESCENT GIRLS EMPOWERMENT &amp; PROTECTI DCD 35443 SLE.IRC.2024.01</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Adolescent Girls Empowerment and Protection Project, implemented by International Rescue Committee with local patrtners, aims to ensure that adolescent girls in Sierra Leone are empowered and motivated through relevant education, knowledge, skills, and inclusive participation in decision-making within their family and society. The project directly targets 1200 adolescent girls. The project also supports 500 women in with Women Action Groups (WAGs) in communities on GBV prevention and response, case management and referral; and works with 400 men and 450 boys; and other community members on transforming gender norms.</narrative>
  </description>
